    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0403" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b W 52/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-17T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Department has received report from our Legation at Lisbon<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d169-f1"/> that the contract of the Western Union regarding cable
                    landing in the Azores is expected to be issued from the Senate Monday, February
                    19, and to be sent back to the Chamber in order to have the amendment deleted.
                    Final approval is expected as soon as this is <pb facs="0404" n="280"
                        xml:id="pg280"/> done. The Legation believes it will be extremely helpful to
                    have British pressure withdrawn. Recently this pressure has been renewed with
                    greater intensity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
